// Require a supported OS version.
//
// Thresholds are reviewed with each major OS release; last updated
// 2026-06-21.
//
// macOS floors at 14.0.0, a deliberately lenient N-2: as of June 2026,
// macOS 26 "Tahoe" is current, 15.x "Sequoia" is N-1, and 14.x "Sonoma" is
// N-2, which the floor accepts to avoid disrupting Sonoma users mid-cycle.
// `os_version_num` encodes the marketing version reported by
// `sw_vers -productVersion` (14.0.0 becomes 14000000). Darwin kernel
// versions (25.x) are NOT what this compares.
//
// Windows floors at build 26100 (24H2) and is compared by `os_build_num`,
// the registry `CurrentBuild` value. It cannot use `os_version_num`: the
// Windows CLI reports a 4-component `os_version` ("10.0.26100.0") that the
// version encoding rejects, yielding -1.
//
// Linux satisfies neither branch and is therefore denied: distributions
// version independently, so no single built-in threshold is meaningful. An
// org running Linux should leave this policy off and add a custom one, e.g.
// `context.device.os_distribution == "ubuntu" &&
//  context.device.os_version_num >= 22004000`.
@id("os_recency")
forbid (principal, action == Vouch::Action::"IssueToken", resource)
unless {
    (context.device.os == "macos" && context.device.os_version_num >= 14000000) ||
    (context.device.os == "windows" && context.device.os_build_num >= 26100)
};
